near its intraday high, suggesting the underlying bid remains intact.\n\nThe structure story over the past month is one of base-building followed by a controlled advance. Price found a floor around the 183.60\u2013184.00 region in early July, bounced, and then spent roughly a week consolidating in the 184.50\u2013185.70 corridor before breaking higher with intent around 14\u201315 July. Since then, the daily closes have been progressively firmer, with the 186.44 high from 23 July now acting as a near-term reference point that has been retested and, on today's session, edged above. The desk identifies four key zones below current price. The 186.21 prior reaction zone \u2014 tested on three separate occasions \u2014 has transitioned into the first meaningful support shelf. Beneath that, the 185.98 area has seen four touches and represents a more substantial structural anchor. Further down, 185.82 and 185.24 mark progressively deeper structure supports that would need to give way before the broader bullish read is materially questioned.\n\nOn the H1 chart, the intraday narrative is one of quiet accumulation. Price dipped to the 185.90 area during the early hours of the Asian session, found willing buyers, and has since grinded steadily higher through the European morning. The 186.40\u2013186.45 band offered mild resistance through the early London hours before being absorbed, with the pair printing a session high of 186.74 during the 05:00 candle before settling into a tight range between 186.52 and 186.63. The current consolidation just below 186.55 has the hallmarks of digestion rather than distribution, with wicks contained and closes clustered.\n\nThe economic calendar carries no scheduled releases of note today, which removes the prospect of sharp data-driven volatility but also means any directional move will be driven by positioning flows or broader risk sentiment. A quiet calendar can sometimes allow cleaner technical reads, but it equally means thin conditions could amplify any unexpected headline risk.\n\nThe bullish read remains intact so long as price holds above the 186.21 prior reaction zone on a daily closing basis. A failure to hold that level, and particularly a close beneath 185.98, would shift the narrative toward a more neutral or corrective interpretation. A sustained push and close above the 186.74 intraday high would represent a fresh structural development worth monitoring.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}